From b08604931d7d51315e899a3cd1390e8c37a5c905 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 19:38:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02422/11362] [outer-loop] add a deepcopy-per-node branch mode
 to OfflineSolver (opt-in, additive)

OfflineSolver.solve_level navigates between search nodes by replay-from-reset
(env.reset() + re-apply the path). For games whose env state is fully a function
of the action prefix that works (lp85, sc25). Added an OPT-IN "deepcopy" branch
mode (branch_mode kwarg, default "replay" -> behaviour UNCHANGED) that instead
snapshots copy.deepcopy(env._game) per node and restores by deepcopy, branching
the EXACT env state rather than reconstructing it -- for games where
replay-from-reset doesn't faithfully reproduce the searched state.

Each heap node carries its (snapshot, frame) so state_key/verifier see the right
frame; the found path is the same shape (a label sequence), so the reproduction
gate is unchanged.

VALIDATED on lp85 (a deepcopy-injectable env): replay and deepcopy modes produce
the IDENTICAL reproducing result (L3, 38 moves, reproduced=True) -- the mode is
correct. Plumbed via a new GameAdapter.branch_mode field (default "replay")
through solve_adaptered, so a future game can opt in.

NB tu93 does NOT benefit: its env is NOT deepcopy-injectable (gotcha #3 --
deepcopy-injection works for lp85, breaks for sc25 and, it turns out, tu93), and
it separately has a replay-search bug graph_explore doesn't hit; both are
distinct from this mode. So no game opts into "deepcopy" yet -- the mode is the
substrate for ones that need it.

2 branch-mode unit tests (toy deterministic game: both modes agree + reproduce;
default is "replay"); 20 ARC tests pass; ruff + spec-coverage clean. lp85 replay
path unchanged (conductor PHASE-C untouched).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
